WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.375
Each thread reads a token and atomically

00:00:03.375 --> 00:00:05.838
increments its selected counter. In this

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.302
case all thirty-two tokens select counter

00:00:08.302 --> 00:00:08.713
two.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.912
All counters start at zero. What will

00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:18.225
counter two contain after all thirty-two

00:00:18.225 --> 00:00:18.610
updates?

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.386
Counter two contains thirty-two. Every

00:00:29.386 --> 00:00:31.206
atomic update is counted.

00:00:35.706 --> 00:00:37.696
With an ordinary increment, two threads

00:00:37.696 --> 00:00:40.349
could both read zero and both write one.

00:00:40.349 --> 00:00:43.002
Two increments would leave a count of one.
